A||||33||TRiAD||Interest in SC kit for 2.8?||||1||
Z||000000||TRiAD||10-19-2001||04:32 PM||||I'm planning on developing a bolt-on supercharger kit for the stock GT engine before it hits the pile in favor of something more stout (3800SC? LT1? Z06? You won't know till it's complete  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ). I am nearly done making a kit for another application, and will have a loose supercharger and an available donor (as soon as I find a cheap GT, see other post).<P>I will test the kit at 6, 8 and 10psi, and will keep it under $3K. <BR>My question is this, if the motor will withstand the psi, who would be interested in a kit that would be based on the Eaton blower and would add 60-100HP (different pulleys, fuel upgrades, etc)?<P>email triadtuning@hotmail.com or respond in this thread. <P>Thanks! <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Brandon86SE||10-19-2001||04:37 PM||||Just to let you know, <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/main.html" TARGET=_blank>RS Motorsports</A> in Canada is already making a 80hp kit for the stock 2.8, and sells it for about $1500US.  I haven't heard any testing results or anything on it, or heard from anyone using their setup, but just thought I should let you know.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||04:43 PM||||Ummm... $1500?  I don't see that on thier Fiero Catalog page.  I see a 2.8 SC for $3199 USD/$4499 Canadian.  Am I missing something?<BR> <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm</A> <P>Also, it doesn't allow you to keep your A/C... I know I'd pass on any upgrade that looses my A/C- something to keep in mind.<P>Oh yeah, this link takes you to their frames page that has the directional controls for the site: <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A> <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||10-19-2001||04:45 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B>Just to let you know, <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/main.html" TARGET=_blank>RS Motorsports</A> in Canada is already making a 80hp kit for the stock 2.8, and sells it for about $1500US.  I haven't heard any testing results or anything on it, or heard from anyone using their setup, but just thought I should let you know.<P>Brandon<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yes they sell one but its $4499or $(US)3199<BR>not $1500.  Also they recommend a rebuild with more stout componets.  Oh and its only for cars with no AC<BR><p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brandon86SE||10-19-2001||04:47 PM||||ok, sorry about that guys it had actually been a while since I checked the cost, but I think it did go up if it's what you're saying.  I remember reading it for like $2500, thought that was the Canadian cost, but must've been the American.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||10-19-2001||04:52 PM||||Thanks for the info...<P>Here's the info on their kit, from their page...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><I>"SUPERCHARGER FOR 2.8 V6 FIERO fits standard or auto 85-88 V6 Fieros with no A/C. <BR>NOW AVAILABLE WITH VORTECH CHARGER, MAX 20 PSI<BR>Complete bolt-on kit, 80HP increase, 200HP output on stock motor<BR>at the WHEELS at 9PSI..<BR>Installation takes about 8 hrs, have to put an adapter in the oil pan for the supercharger oil drain, bolt on the sc bracket, oil-pressure line and sensor adapters, supercharger unit, oil lines, install induction pipes, blow-off valve (vacum controlled), change the MAP sensor and the ECU with the ones we supply (plugs in) and you are ready to gooooooo....<BR>Options include a Greddy blow-off valve and boost&air/fuel gauge."</I><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Here's the differences...<BR>Mine will work with AC <BR>Mine will use an Eaton blower, way more relaible, and you don't need to tap into anything for oil, their Vortech is basically a belt-driven turbo, lag and all. <BR>You also won't need a "blow-off" valve on mine, because it only makes the pressure you want, none of this "20psi" crap. <BR>Eaton's will also make power FROM IDLE, whereas a centrifugal (Vortech, Paxton, etc) will need to spin up to speed. <BR>My Eaton kit will include a bypass, so it will only use 0.6HP when you're not in boost, which will be whenever you're at less than 75% throttle. This saves wear and tear, gas mileage, etc...<BR>Mine will also take more like 4 hours to install, judging from my other applications. <P>There's a reason Mercedes, Jaguar, GM, Ford...all use Eatons.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||04:55 PM||||You've certainly peaked my curiousity... keep me posted.<P>(now only to decide... Turbo, SuperCharger, SC 3800 Series II, or Archie LT1 V8... maybe the pocketbook with have some say in this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000007||falconhulk||10-19-2001||04:56 PM||||heh heh heh come on man are you serious?????  If so I would plunk that money down so fast and hard it would break the table.  $3000????????? <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||TRiAD||10-19-2001||05:29 PM||||<I> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Are you serious?</I><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dead serious...<BR>I have the charger sitting here...and a second party locally who custom builds manifolds, and brackets. I always make the belt an easy part to replace, both in placement and in spec (usually a Honda belt). <BR>...All I need is the GT and some time...about 2 weeks should being it to the table, and another 4 or so to be viable for retail. <BR>Gotta buy the car first.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's nice to see all the interest!||||reg||1
