Z||000013||Voytek||10-19-2001||06:36 PM||||DXR - I only see one thumb.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Triad - a definite interest here.  <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>wow...sounds sweet, will you keep making them for a while? im more than willing to pay that much, but i dont have it, or wont for a little while..just wondering if ull still be making them when i can afford em.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's a good question.  I have some body mods planned for this winter.  A turbo?  Probably not till mid-to-later next year, but if available, I would definitely be interested.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||TRiAD||10-19-2001||07:05 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><I>"Will you keep making them..."</I><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Once the kit is developed, the only custom parts would be the brackets and manifold, and add the charger itself and the belt, pulley, harware, fuel system upgrade and gauges...There's no problem in continuing to offer the kit indefinitely. <P>As for location and actual mounting, stay tuned...this is part of the development and will be tackled once the car is here. It is in the design stage however. <P><I>(and Voytek, you do realise this is a belt-driven supercharger and not an exhaust-driven turbo, right? FYI)</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
